Third-party notice for internal/mosh
====================================

The terminal/ package is a Go port of the client-side terminal model in stock
mosh 1.4.0: src/terminal (parser, emulator, framebuffer, dispatcher, display,
and user input), src/statesync/completeterminal.cc, and
src/frontend/terminaloverlay.cc. The parity driver and committed goldens under
terminal/testdata/parity are built from or produced by that stock code.

  Source: https://github.com/mobile-shell/mosh/releases/download/mosh-1.4.0/mosh-1.4.0.tar.gz
  SHA-256: 872e4b134e5df29c8933dff12350785054d2fd2839b5ae6b5587b14db1465ddd
  Copyright (C) 2012 Keith Winstein and mosh contributors
  License: GNU General Public License, version 3 or later

This port is distributed as part of the same GPL-3.0-or-later work. The Docker
parity harness downloads and builds the stock source at image-build time; no
stock mosh source or binary is committed to this repository. The harness
provenance and source hash are recorded in
terminal/testdata/parity/harness/README.md.

The OCB3 implementation in ocb.go is adapted from mosh-go:

  Repository: https://github.com/unixshells/mosh-go
  Tag: v0.5.2
  Commit: 0284bd652aab3dfff5b0b74945c23901d7537b61
  Copyright (c) 2026 Unix Shells
  License: MIT

The wire framing, protobuf field numbers, fragment handling, and SSP behavior
were implemented against the mosh project's protocol and source code with the
same reference implementation as a guide. This package is distributed as part
of a GPL-3.0-or-later work; the MIT license below continues to apply to the
adapted portions.

